# motion-craft

Ten commands. Each runs with a clear input contract, a sequence of skill calls, and an output contract.

| Command | Trigger | Output |
|---|---|---|
| **init** | "set up motion for this project" | `MOTION.md` + Design Read |
| **shape** | "plan motion before coding" | storyboard of beats + recipe + dial values |
| **animate** | "implement the animations" | GSAP code matching recipe + motion mode |
| **polish** | "polish this", "final pass" | tightened durations / eases / staggers + reduced-motion branch |
| **audit** | "audit", "lint", "remove the slop" | structured report from motion-anti-slop |
| **critique** | "design review" | qualitative review (does motion serve content?) |
| **quieter** | "tone this down" | one-step reduction along Restrained → Expressive → Cinematic |
| **bolder** | "amplify", "boring" | one-step amplification with discipline |
| **adapt** | "make it accessible", "responsive" | `gsap.matchMedia` + breakpoint-aware motion |
| **export** | "export as transparent video", "render to webm" | `capture.js` (Puppeteer) + FFmpeg commands |

Composable: `init` → `shape` → `animate` → `polish` → `audit`.

For each command's exact Sequence and Output contract: see `skills/motion-craft/SKILL.md`.
